  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Postcolonial Realms of Memory (2020), published by Liverpool University Press, has been cited 10 times — enough that OpenAlex puts it in the top 10% of works in its field and year. Beyond that, it is used in teaching.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Postcolonial Realms of Memory by Etienne Achille, Charles Forsdick and Lydie Moudileno was published by Liverpool University Press in 2020. Conceptually, the work connects to Colonialism, Collective memory, Inscribed figure, Historiography and History.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 10 citations. That places it in the top 10% of works in its field and year of publication. Citations peaked in 2023 with 3 citing works. Notable citing venues include Revue française d’études américaines, E-rea and Politička revija. The citing works include 6 journal articles, 3 book chapters and 1 review. They come from 7 countries, led by the United Kingdom, France and Australia.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 1 recorded lecture. Open Library reports a combined count of 2 reading logs and catalog editions. Its subject matter aligns with Sustainable cities and communities among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\" data-wiki-books=\"verified\">The latest English Wikipedia check verified 3 article–work reference matches. These are references or bibliography entries, which may include other editions of the same work; they do not measure readership.</p>\n",
